2026-06-28 02:36:02,624 | INFO | HTTP Request: POST http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/chat "HTTP/1.1 200 OK"
2026-06-28 02:36:02,624 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: To address the client's requirements, we will implement several security controls based on our existing capabilities. 

Firstly, we are already ISO 27001 certified, which demonstrates our commitment to information security management. Our scope of certification includes development, delivery, and operations.

Regarding GDPR compliance, we have ISO 27701 certification, which is an extension for privacy information management. This ensures that we have the necessary controls in place to handle personal data securely. 

For data protection measures, we use encryption in transit (TLS 1.3) and at rest (AES-256), with key management handled on EU-based infrastructure. We also implement strict partitioning of client files with logical isolation per client and per mission, preventing any cross-client circulation of data. Pseudonymisation is used where applicable, and we adhere to the principle of data minimization.

To ensure explainability and auditability, our product Atelier provides grounded and traceable outputs. It also supports internal quality control and statutory audit review. 

We have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and maintain a data processing register. Our data processing agreement (DPA) is aligned with GDPR Article 28.

For security controls specifically, we follow a secure software development life cycle (SDLC), which includes code reviews, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing by an external provider of equivalent CREST level. We also have vulnerability management with remediation SLAs based on severity and an incident response plan in place, including detection, notification, and remediation.

Our hosting partner is OuraneCloud, where we hold the SecNumCloud qualification at the hosting layer, supporting sovereign hosting of confidential data within the EU. This ensures that all data remains within the EU and is not transferred outside, complying with GDPR requirements for data sovereignty.

Lastly, we ensure segregation of duties between development and production operations and have controls in place to prevent unauthorized access or changes to sensitive data.

By implementing these security controls, we can ensure compliance with the client's regulatory requirements, including strict GDPR adherence, explainability and audibility of AI outputs, and adherence to accounting standards and other relevant regulations.
